# `engine-strict` is deliberately NOT set here.
#
# It sounds like the right way to refuse an unsupported Node, and it is too blunt: it applies
# to every transitive dependency as well, so one dev dependency that has not yet declared
# support for a current Node blocks every install in the project. firebase-tools pulls in
# `superstatic`, which is exactly that.
#
# The guarantee is kept where it can be precise. `make doctor` checks Node against this
# project's own `engines`, and the `node_modules` target checks it again before `npm ci` — so
# an unsupported version still cannot get as far as installing, and says why. Getting that
# wrong is expensive: on the wrong Node, jsdom mishandles localStorage and what you see is
# two dozen storage tests failing with nothing pointing at Node.
